I'm still trying (now and then, when I get a chance) to get the X11
version of nethack 3.1.3 compiled on my HP 425 with HP-UX 8.0.

I've finally managed to get the fonts installed (when using xset +fp 
I had to use the full path name, and the directory had to be globally
readable, otherwise I got a meaningless error message).

Next problem, my X11 include files are in /usr/include/X11R4/X11.  The
X11 installation files says:

>If your X11 include files and libraries are not installed in a standard
>place (i.e. /usr/include/X11 and /usr/lib respectively) you will need to
>prepend an appropriate -I<idirectory> parameter to CFLAGS and a
>-L<ldirectory> parameter to LFLAGS, setting <?directory> to the place to
>find the include and library files for X11.

OK, I edit the Makefile, and set:
CFLAGS = -g -I/usr/include/X11R4 ../include
LFLAGS = -L/usr/lib/X11R4

Unfortunately, while it now finds the X11 directory, it no longer finds the
../include directory.  So (thinking cleverly) I put it back to:
CFLAGS = -g -I ../include
  and created a link from my include directory to the X11 directory (ie:
ln -s /usr/include/X11R4/X11 ../include/X11).  This works, and it finds 
all the include files (but I wouldn't mind knowing what I really should 
have set the CFLAGS to).

My next problem currently has me stumped.  The next error message I got
when compiling was:
        cc -g -I../include  -c ../win/X11/dialogs.c
../win/X11/dialogs.c: 52: Can't find include file X11/Xaw/Cardinals.h
../win/X11/dialogs.c: 53: Can't find include file X11/Xaw/Form.h
../win/X11/dialogs.c: 54: Can't find include file X11/Xaw/Label.h
../win/X11/dialogs.c: 55: Can't find include file X11/Xaw/AsciiText.h
../win/X11/dialogs.c: 56: Can't find include file X11/Xaw/Command.h
*** Error code 1

I looked under the X11 directory, and there was no Xaw subdirectory.
I couldn't find those files anywhere.  Does anyone know what they are,
or where I can get them for my machine?

I pretty much stuck for now.  If no one can help, I think I may wait 
until I get upgraded to X11R5 and HP-UX9.0 (which I think is happening 
"soon") and try again then.  For now, I'm stuck with TTY.
